Harmattan: no Qt NFC

Qt 5.15's only Linux NFC backend talks to neard, which the N9 doesn't have (its NFC stack
is Nokia's own), so on the linux-harmattan-g++ mkspec Qt NFC isn't built: a module that
never finds a reader. Qt Bluetooth builds as usual (BlueZ 4 over D-Bus, classic only).

--- a/src/src.pro
+++ b/src/src.pro
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 TEMPLATE = subdirs
 
-SUBDIRS += bluetooth nfc
+SUBDIRS += bluetooth
+# Nokia N9/N950: no NFC. Qt's only Linux backend is neard; the phone's NFC stack is Nokia's.
+!linux-harmattan-g++: SUBDIRS += nfc
 android {
     SUBDIRS += android
     android.depends += bluetooth nfc
@@ -17,7 +19,8 @@
 }
 
 qtHaveModule(quick) {
-    imports.depends += bluetooth nfc
+    imports.depends += bluetooth
+    contains(SUBDIRS, nfc): imports.depends += nfc
     SUBDIRS += imports
 }
 
